  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict (24-hour reporting and notice, covering all incidents without waiting for cause confirmation), which hurts both companies given their unreported incidents. S2 and S3 favour Northwind: S2 has no sales stop for models above 5%, which protects the Hearth 10, and S3 sets a 24-month new-unit deadline and a retrofit no earlier than six years, which suits Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage. S5 applies an 8/100k mandatory recall with no transition, which forces a recall of Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9/100k, while S4's 36-month suppression deadline is more favourable to Halcyon's higher suppression cost."
